---
description: STRATO Convention Lead Generation engineering constraints
alwaysApply: true
---

- Use Next.js App Router and TypeScript strict mode.
- Follow the product requirements and UI/UX design spec in the root Markdown files.
- Keep server-only integrations in route handlers or server-only modules.
- Never expose secrets through `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`, client components, logs, or API responses.
- Validate every untrusted request on the server.
- `Other` product interest requires a non-empty Comment.
- The product-interest choices and ordering must match the requirements exactly.
- Leads must be written to the private Google Sheet only. Do not send notification email. Never fake success in production.
- Business cards must be configurable through the protected admin interface, not hardcoded per employee.
- Only active cards are publicly listed or retrievable.
- Generate a valid vCard file and QR code using the deployed canonical URL.
- Do not invent STRATO branding assets, customer logos, metrics, or staff details.
- Keep the UI mobile-first, accessible, and enterprise-professional.
- Include loading, empty, success, error, and unavailable states.
- Prefer small reusable components and clear types.
- Do not suppress TypeScript/lint errors as a shortcut.
- Do not add paid third-party APIs unless explicitly approved.
- Run lint, typecheck, tests, and production build before declaring a phase complete.
